    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">electoral process</span> is the set of procedures by which citizens choose their representatives and leaders. Free, fair, and credible elections are the cornerstone of democratic governance.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. INEC and Electoral Administration</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">The Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) was established by the 1999 Constitution to organise, supervise, and monitor elections in Nigeria. INEC: registers voters, accredits parties, conducts elections, declares results, and registers/deregisters parties. The Chairman of INEC is appointed by the President subject to Senate confirmation.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Electoral Systems</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Description</th><th>Nigeria's Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>First-Past-The-Post (FPTP)</td><td>Candidate with most votes wins</td><td>Used for most Nigerian elections (House of Reps, governorship)</td></tr><tr><td>Proportional Representation (PR)</td><td>Seats allocated proportional to votes</td><td>Not used in Nigeria; common in Europe</td></tr><tr><td>Two-Round System</td><td>If no majority in first round, run-off between top two</td><td>Not used in Nigeria</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Requirements for Voting in Nigeria</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li>Nigerian citizenship</li><li>Age: 18 years and above</li><li>Registration with INEC and possession of Permanent Voter's Card (PVC)</li><li>Not currently serving a prison sentence</li><li>Not certified as insane</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Electoral Malpractice</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Forms: ballot stuffing, rigging, voter intimidation, falsification of results, multiple voting, underage voting, vote-buying. Consequences: undermines democracy, leads to poor governance, creates political instability.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Election Tribunal</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Petition courts for disputing election results. Nigeria's election petition tribunals are time-limited (180 days maximum) and have specific procedures.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span><strong>INEC Chairman appointment:</strong> Appointed by the President on the recommendation of the Council of State, subject to Senate confirmation. Serves 5-year term, non-renewable.</div><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span><strong>Summary:</strong> INEC administers elections. Voting: 18+, Nigerian citizen, PVC, not imprisoned or insane. FPTP used in Nigeria. Presidential win: majority + 25% in 24 states. Electoral malpractice undermines democracy.</div>",
