    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Conflict</span> is a situation of disagreement or incompatibility between parties. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">War</span> is armed conflict between states or organised groups. Understanding causes, types, and resolution of conflicts is essential for international relations.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Types of Conflict</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li><strong>Interstate conflict:</strong> between sovereign states (conventional war)</li><li><strong>Intrastate/Civil conflict:</strong> within a state (civil war, insurgency)</li><li><strong>Non-state conflict:</strong> involving armed groups without state backing</li><li><strong>Proxy war:</strong> conflict where major powers support opposing sides without direct military engagement</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Causes of International Conflict</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li>Territorial disputes and boundary problems</li><li>Competition for resources (oil, water, minerals)</li><li>Ethnic, religious, and cultural differences</li><li>Political ideology and power competition</li><li>Economic inequality and injustice</li><li>Historical grievances and nationalism</li><li>Colonially imposed artificial borders (especially in Africa)</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Conflict Resolution Methods</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li><strong>Negotiation:</strong> direct talks between parties</li><li><strong>Mediation:</strong> neutral third party facilitates agreement</li><li><strong>Arbitration:</strong> binding decision by a neutral third party</li><li><strong>Adjudication:</strong> settlement by an international court (ICJ)</li><li><strong>Peacekeeping/Enforcement:</strong> military deployment to maintain peace</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span><strong>Nigeria's internal conflicts:</strong> Nigerian Civil War (1967-1970, Biafra secession attempt). Current: Boko Haram insurgency (Northeast), banditry (Northwest), IPOB agitation (Southeast), farmer-herder conflicts.</div><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span><strong>Summary:</strong> Conflict causes: territory, resources, ethnicity, ideology. Types: interstate, civil, proxy. Resolution: negotiation, mediation, arbitration, ICJ adjudication. Nigerian Civil War 1967-70. Boko Haram from 2009.</div>",
